From 0ee0b10a688dd6f76bf7f27c3b265ba9dace47cb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 18:04:39 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Add experimental libhegel backend and engine through
 hegeltest's binding

Two experiments towards sharing one engine with libhegel, the native
engine behind the Hegel libraries, reached through hegel._native, the
pyo3 extension of Hegel's own Python frontend (the hegeltest package, an
optional dependency: hypothesis[hegel]). No Rust is added to Hypothesis.

backend="hegel" is a PrimitiveProvider whose draw_* go to libhegel one to
one (weighted and shrink_towards integers, NaN with finite bounds,
alphabets as explicit codepoint ranges, forced draws recorded in the
engine's sequence), with replay-equivalence tests: a Hypothesis choice
sequence encoded as a libhegel blob replays through libhegel value for
value.

HYPOTHESIS_ENGINE=hegel makes core.py build a HegelRunner instead of
ConjectureRunner for tests on the default backend: libhegel owns the run
loop, generation, shrinking, targeting and the choice budget, Python
keeps ConjectureData, test execution and reporting; libhegel's run
errors map onto Unsatisfiable, the health checks and FlakyFailure by
kind. hegel_ir.py compiles the declarative built-in strategies
(integers, floats, booleans, binary, text, lists, tuples, fixed
dictionaries, one_of, sampled_from, just, map, builds, filter) into the
tree hegel._native's interpreter walks in one call, mirroring each
do_draw, with opaque leaves handed back to ConjectureData.draw for
everything else; ConjectureData consults the provider's draw_strategy
first, records the choices the interpreter made, and tells a provider
about the draws Hypothesis forces. The equivalence check: for each kind
of strategy, a natively generated value is exactly what the Python
engine draws when it replays libhegel's recorded choices through its own
do_draw code. HYPOTHESIS_HEGEL_BATCH=0 keeps every draw interactive.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_016mTrLpQ8SJg9RC9F1GH9Ac
