+RELEASE_TYPE: minor
+
+This release adds two experiments towards sharing one engine with
+`libhegel <https://hegel.dev/reference/libhegel>`__, the native engine behind
+the Hegel family of property-based testing libraries, reached through the
+``hegeltest`` package (Hegel's own Python frontend, ``pip install
+hypothesis[hegel]``). ``backend="hegel"`` generates inputs with it while
+everything else stays in Python, and setting ``HYPOTHESIS_ENGINE=hegel`` in
+the environment hands it the whole run loop, including shrinking and
+targeting, for tests on the default backend, generating whole values of the
+built-in strategies natively where it can. Neither is a supported feature:
+both may change or disappear in any release, and the engine flag ignores the
+example database for now.
